{
  "abstract": "Positive and signed arithmetic profiles over ordered separated pairs of multiplicative runs, including both moving residue phases and the explicit two-channel probability law. Every fixed finite channel-height truncation has a literal next-height cumulant and law remainder and a sharp total-variation equivalent. Weighted nonaligned pairs, the closed height-five correction, and the height-six phase are included with their exact coefficients.",
